  "final_message": "I'll start by reading the benchmark instructions and the task list so I know exactly what to solve.The language reference has several non-obvious rules, so I\u2019ll check those with the toolchain before writing the solutions.Arithmetic and indexing don\u2019t follow the usual rules, so the solutions will use explicit floor division and 1-based indexes. Next I\u2019ll implement every task and test it.All 17 tasks are solved in `solutions/` and checked against the sample cases plus extra edges: calendar dates, signed floor division, Game of Life, big multiplication, and the RPN error cases.\n\nWhat tripped me up was that every binary operator shares one precedence and groups left to right, so a product has to be parenthesized or it is computed too late. Division rounds toward positive infinity, which makes the remainder of an odd number negative, and the two operands of an operator are evaluated right to left. Indexes start at 1 and wrap around the collection, and there is no if statement: every branch is a conditional jump to a label.",
